## 5. OAuth 2.0 & Identity Provider Alignment

When moving from `localhost` to a Cloudflare HTTPS hostname, external identity providers must be configured with the exact callback URL generated by n8n.

### 5.1 Google Cloud Platform (GCP) Credentials Setup

1. Open **GCP Console** > **APIs & Services** > **Credentials**.
2. Edit the relevant **OAuth 2.0 Client ID** configured as a Web Application.
3. Under **Authorized redirect URIs**, add the n8n callback URL:

```text
https://customise-dow-surprising-meet.trycloudflare.com/rest/oauth2-credential/callback
```

4. Save the configuration.

> The hostname must match the current n8n public URL exactly, including HTTPS and the callback path.

### 5.2 n8n Credential Synchronization

1. Open the n8n dashboard through the Cloudflare URL:

```text
https://customise-dow-surprising-meet.trycloudflare.com
```

2. Go to **Settings > Credentials**.
3. Open the **Gmail OAuth2 API** credential.
4. Confirm that the displayed OAuth Redirect URL is:

```text
https://customise-dow-surprising-meet.trycloudflare.com/rest/oauth2-credential/callback
```

5. Use **Reconnect / Switch account** and complete the Google authorization flow.

