## 7. Troubleshooting & Verification

| Issue | Likely Cause | Solution |
|---|---|---|
| Console output appears stalled or incomplete | QUIC/UDP transport behavior on the Windows console/network | Retry with `--protocol http2` for the Quick Tunnel command |
| `redirect_uri_mismatch` | OAuth provider callback URL does not exactly match n8n's current public callback URL | Synchronize the exact HTTPS callback URL in GCP and n8n |
| Cloudflare dashboard shows `0 Routes` | Tunnel exists but no public hostname/published application route is configured | Add a published application and map it to `http://localhost:5678` |
| n8n webhooks still use `localhost` | Public URL environment configuration is missing or stale | Update `WEBHOOK_URL` to the current public HTTPS hostname and restart n8n |
| Quick Tunnel URL stopped working | Quick Tunnel was temporary or the `cloudflared` process exited | Restart the Quick Tunnel and update the n8n/OAuth URLs |
| OAuth works locally but not through Cloudflare | Provider only has the localhost redirect URI registered | Add the exact Cloudflare HTTPS callback URI to the OAuth client configuration |
| Browser reaches Cloudflare but n8n is unavailable | Local n8n service is stopped or port `5678` is not reachable from the host | Verify the container is running and `http://localhost:5678` works locally |

